-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be finite with decidable equality, let $r\le k$, and let $P$ be an ordered coarse-fine complex. Fix a full tuple $x$ and real tolerance functions $\alpha,\beta$. If the face tuple of $x$ avoids the source-full top bad-base deletion for every ordered $r$-face, the canonical closed atom configuration induced by $x$ in the coarse complex is source-full mixed-good for $P,\alpha,\beta$.
